t to the data  in  in years less than 2005  and now when we come to predict  we're going to predict on the  the remaining data which is years 2005  or greater  and  so we use a predict function again  and for the new data we give it s market  but indexed by not trained so that's  going to be  not trained is  it's going to be  true if if year is 2005 or more  and we tell a type equals response so we  actually want to predict  the the probabilities in this case  and again we make this if else if  make this up down variable  and let's make a subset  a new variable direction.2005  again for the test data which is  the response variable direction  which is just for the test dates in  other words not train so we call that  direction.2005  and now we make a table so now this is  on test data there's a smaller subset of  the data is test  and we compute our mean again and it's  0.48 so now we've actually done  gets slightly less than 50 percent  so  it's  we'd be doing worse than the  the null rate which is 50  so  what are we going to do well we might  for this we might be overfitting and  that's why we're doing worse on the on  the on the test data  so now we're going to fit a smaller  model  so  we're going to just use lag 1 and lag 2  and leave out all the other variables  and so  here we do that the rest of the calls  the same  and then we run through our commands  again  we compute our table  and here we get an error rate of of 55  a correct classification of just about  56  which is not too bad at all  and  so  using the smaller model appears to have  done better here and if we do a summary  of that guy  let's see if anything became significant  by using the smaller model  that it gave us better predictions  and of course that's what happens when  you try and do commands on the type on  the fly at least for me you make  spelling mistakes  well nothing became significant but at  least the prediction of performance  appeared to have improved  so that's for the logistic regression  models in r using the glm function and  family equals binomial

